            'SET INDUCTION: 5 minutes\n1. Teacher ensures pupils are seated appropriately and have the required stationery.\n2. Teacher distributes the assessment paper and explains the general instructions without discussing answers.\n3. Pupils write the required details and listen to the instructions.',
            'MAIN ACTIVITIES: Assessment session\n1. Pupils read the instructions for each section carefully.\n2. Pupils answer the assessment individually within the allocated time.\n3. Teacher supervises the assessment, maintains examination conditions and only clarifies administrative instructions when necessary.\n4. Teacher gives an appropriate time reminder before the session ends.\n5. Pupils check that all required questions have been attempted.',
            'CLOSURE: 5 minutes\n1. Teacher instructs pupils to stop writing when the allocated time ends.\n2. Pupils submit their scripts in an orderly manner.\n3. Teacher checks that all scripts have been collected.',
